From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:53:51 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] engine: child reports follow one rule: the first turn
 after the parent's message answers it

The person's Stop is filed in the parent's ledger, never read by its agent, and what they write next carries on the task; another agent's Stop reports at once. A run the engine's own shutdown cut reports when revived, or as failed on the next start, which now runs after every recovery and has no 1 h limit. One follow-up at most, only when the end left background work running and once it is done. At the parent, a working child's message waits for its end, and an answered question is dropped. Devices say child-reports in their capabilities.
