+The parent's message opens a request, and the first turn of the child's that
+settles after it answers it and reports, whoever wrote to the child meanwhile
+(the person's word to a working child corrects the task). Once it's answered,
+a turn the person starts in the child is theirs. The person's Stop doesn't
+answer it: it's kept in the parent's ledger (`…-stopped-quiet`), never read by
+its agent, and the turn after what the person writes next reports. A Stop by
+another chat's agent reports at once; the parent's own doesn't. A turn cut off
+by Zeron shutting down reports when the next start revives it, or as failed.
+An engine with this rule says so in its device's capabilities
+(`child-reports`).
+
+When the end said the child left work running in its background, the first
+turn it starts on its own once that work is done reports once more, opening
+with `(Follow-up: …)`; turns while it runs, and any after, don't. A report
+whose reply repeats what the child already sent its parent with
+`send_message` says so instead of the words. A short, tool-free answer to the
+parent's short thanks after a report is kept in the parent's ledger
+(`…-quiet`) and never read by its agent. At the parent, a child's message on
+the way waits for that child's end while it still works (a minute at most),
+and a question answered meanwhile is dropped. A report that comes in after
 the person stopped the parent still wakes it; the person's own queued messages
 stay paused.
 
